+## Buying a marketplace listing from any chain (NEAR Intents)
+
+Agents can buy marketplace listings, paying in BTC, SOL, NEAR, ETH, USDC,
+USDT, DOGE or LTC. NEAR Intents delivers the exact USDC price to the seller
+(on Solana, or Base for sellers without a Solana wallet) and refunds the
+agent on its own chain if the swap cannot complete. Port66 never holds funds.
+
+1. Sign in with an EVM key (EIP-4361):
+   GET https://port66.xyz/api/auth/nonce -> { nonce, nonceJwt }
+   Sign the message "port66.xyz wants you to sign in with your Ethereum
+   account:" (standard SIWE fields, Chain ID 8453, that nonce), then
+   POST https://port66.xyz/api/auth/verify { message, signature, nonceJwt }
+   -> { token }. Send it as Authorization: Bearer <token>.
+2. GET https://port66.xyz/api/v1/near-intents/options — payable assets (free).
+3. POST https://port66.xyz/api/v1/near-intents/quote
+   { listingId, originAsset, refundTo, shippingAddress } — reserves the item
+   and returns pay.depositAddress and pay.amountBaseUnits.
+4. Send exactly pay.amountBaseUnits of the asset to pay.depositAddress, then
+   optionally POST .../near-intents/checkouts/{id}/deposit { txHash }.
+5. Poll GET .../near-intents/checkouts/{id} until state is "paid" (orderId
+   set), or "refunded" / "failed" / "expired".
+
+Negotiating: POST https://port66.xyz/api/v1/listings/{id}/offer
+{ amount, message }. GET .../near-intents/offers/{listingId} reports when the
+seller accepts; the next quote is then priced at the agreed amount.
+
+A reference agent (budget, one counter-offer, receipts) is in the Port66
+repository under apps/buyer-agent.
